{
  "openapi":"3.0.1",
  "info":{
    "title":"TheCondo API",
    "description":"TheCondo is a comprehensive Condominium Management System API.\n\n### Some Possible Actors & Actions\n- **Admin/Manager**: Can create, update, and manage Condominiums, Buildings, Units, Budgets, and set scheduled maintenances. Has full visibility over all payments, expenses, and document management.\n- **Unit Owner**: Can view the status of their unit quotas, handle their specific maintenance requests, view publicly available condominium documents, and check the standings of their own unit ownership.\n- **Resident (Tenant)**: Can view active amenities, book amenities, submit standard maintenance requests, and retrieve non-sensitive general notices or regulations.\n- **Maintenance Staff**: Can view scheduled maintenance events, execute maintenance interventions, update intervention completion statuses, and add progress notes to ongoing interventions. \n\n### Quick Start: How to Explore the API\nTo quickly understand how the data is connected, try clicking these endpoints directly in your browser (they will open the raw JSON responses):\n\n1. **Discover the Hierarchy**: View the top-level organizational structure.\n   [`GET ../api/condominiums`](../api/condominiums) - Returns all condominiums with their nested buildings and units.\n\n2. **Inspect Finances**: Check the financial health of Condo 1.\n   [`GET ../api/condominiums/1/payments/overdue?year=2026`](../api/condominiums/1/payments/overdue?year=2026) - Shows which units are behind on their quotas.\n   [`GET ../api/expenses?condominiumId=1`](../api/expenses?condominiumId=1) - Lists all expenses associated with that specific condominium.\n\n3. **Review Maintenance**: Check up on the building's physical state.\n   [`GET ../api/condominiums/1/maintenance/upcoming?year=2026`](../api/condominiums/1/maintenance/upcoming?year=2026) - A summary of scheduled recurrent maintenance.\n   [`GET ../api/maintenance-requests?condominiumId=1`](../api/maintenance-requests?condominiumId=1) - Displays ad-hoc issues reported by residents.\n\n4. **View Documents**: Explore the hierarchical file management.\n   [`GET ../api/documents/public`](../api/documents/public) - Lists publicly accessible notices and regulations.\n\n### Notes\n- All endpoints are NOT secured and do NOT require authentication. It must be the client's who should create the ilusion of actors roles.\n- The API is designed to be flexible and can be integrated with various front-end applications or mobile apps for condominium management. It already has several condominiums and the data around them so client's may ignore the boilerplate and focus on specific use cases.\n","contact":{"name":"TheCondo Team"},
    "version":"1.0"
  },
